# Grid B — U7 History (churn count in recent window)
#
# Gap target: "how many of the last N commits touched X" is a
# counting + filtering question against git log — there is no
# axis that routes this to git_log as the primary evidence tool.
# The measurement-scalar carve-out does NOT extend to history
# because git_log output is not in the Raw Tool Outputs allowlist
# (context/builder.go skips git_log — verify before shipping).
#
# Ground truth: subject to drift. The case leans on the numeric
# regex to enforce "gave a number" and on the function name to
# enforce scope.
ID="u7b"
NAME="history — recent commits touching runTaskGraph"
QUESTION="最近 20 次修改 internal/orchestrator/ 目录的 commit 中，有多少个直接涉及 runTaskGraph 函数？给出数字。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous regex `\b[0-9]{1,2}\b`
# accepted ANY 1-2 digit number 0-99 (false positive — answers "5"
# or "12" both passed regardless of truth). Ground truth at this
# snapshot (verified via `git log -20 --pretty=format:'%h' --
# internal/orchestrator/ | xargs -I{} git show {} -- internal/
# orchestrator/orchestrator.go | grep runTaskGraph`): 0 commits
# touch runTaskGraph in the last 20 orchestrator/ commits — the
# function body has been stable since the runReadSchedulerLoop
# split. Tighten to `\b[0-2]\b` (small drift tolerance: 0-2) so
# the answer must reflect the actual stability rather than guess.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="runTaskGraph"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="estimate approximately roughly"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="\b[0-2]\b"
